# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FamilyClaw .gitignore — Layer A (OSS) / Layer B (private) boundary
# CRITICAL: no private soul, key, or profile data may ever reach the
# published repo.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Rust build ---
/target
**/target
Cargo.lock.bak
*.pdb

# --- Layer B: private agent profiles and souls (NEVER published) ---
# Profiles are loaded at runtime from the FAMILYCLAW_PROFILE_DIR env var.
/profiles/
profiles/
**/profiles/
*.soul
*.soul.md
SOUL.md
!docs/**/SOUL.md.example
!**/SOUL.example.md
# Private agent identities / memories / calibrations
/hearth/
hearth/
*.calibration.json
emotion-weights*.json
!**/emotion-weights.example.json

# --- Salaisuudet ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*_token*
*api_key*
*API_KEY*
secrets/
*.secret

# --- Lokit, runtime, väliaikaiset ---
*.log
*.pid
/data/
/data2/
*.lance/
/local/
.local/
*.sqlite
*.db
/tmp/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- IDE ---
/.idea/
/.vscode/
*.iml

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Layer B: encoded souls + temporary unpack/debug scripts (NEVER published)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base64-encoded private soul blobs (private journals, calibrations).
*.b64
# Unpacks b64 soul blobs to tar.gz — a private-soul tool, not Layer A code.
recv.py
# Per-session temporary and fix scripts.
tmp-*
fix*.py
fixlib.ps1
# Agent debug/probe scripts (2026-07-14) — self-labeled Layer B in their own
# header comments; one hardcodes a gateway token, so these must never reach
# the Layer A (published) tree. audit-layer-b.sh's secret scan only covers
# crates/*.rs|toml|json and its name scan only covers already-tracked files,
# so untracked scripts/ files like these were never caught by the automated
# audit — quarantined here explicitly instead.
scripts/agent_acceptance_test.py
scripts/agent_clean_memory.py
scripts/probe_tool_calling.ps1
# Rust build intermediates.
*.rlib
# Runtime config binds a private identity + channel; publish only the blanked
# familyclaw.toml.example (allowed below).
familyclaw.toml
# OSS skeleton (empty secret fields) must publish — keep it out of the ignore.
!familyclaw.toml.example
# Python bridge pending a Layer-A/tooling placement decision — kept out for now.
bridge.py

# Night-nudger runtime state (logs, state) — not committed.
.claude/night-nudger-state.json
.claude/night-nudger*.log
.claude/night-nudger-stdout.log
__pycache__/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Layer B: internal planning and research documents
# (NEVER published — contain private agent identities + history.
#  Files stay on disk locally — only removed from Git tracking.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Internal architecture map (private agent identities).
FAMILYCLAW_MAP.md
# Internal plans, research, and source blueprints.
docs/plans/
docs/research/
docs/source-blueprints/
# Internal Layer-B handoff (references private souls + profile paths).
docs/handoff/
# Internal night-run / planning docs (.claude/) with private identities.
# NOTE: only identity-leaking plans — tooling (.py, settings.json) stays.
.claude/NIGHT_RUN_2026-06-11.md
.claude/PLAN_HEARTH.md
# Root-level plan and blueprint documents (private identities + product history).
# These were untracked leak mines.
BLUEPRINT.md
HUIPPUTUOTE_SUUNNITELMA.md
KEHITYSSUUNNITELMA.md
research_plan.md
# Catch-all: any *SUUNNITELMA*.md (plan) is internal by default.
*SUUNNITELMA*.md
NIGHT-FIXES-SUMMARY.md
# Untracked plans with private identities + raw research data + helper script.
FAMILYCLAW_FINAL_PLAN.md
FAMILYCLAW_MASTER_PLAN.md
FAMILYCLAW_TECHNICAL_PLAN.md
research_data.md
papers.txt
write_papers.py
# Package briefs + orchestration that reference private identities (agent
# assignment) → internal, not for Layer A.
PAKETTI-*.md
plans/PARALLEL_RUN_*.md
.claude/night-nudger.py
.claude/usage_meter.py
.claude/PLAN_AAA.md
.claude/PLAN_PERFECT.md
agentit/
core/
ops/
scripts/*.bak-*
plans/
research/
_stray-backup/
PHASE2_RECON_PLAN_*.json

# Experimental Claw language spike (excluded from workspace, WIP) + stray test files
*.claw
/compiler/
# Claw-lang spike spec — references a private agent identity by name (internal).
CLAW_LANG_SPEC.md
# Parallel-build planning doc — references private agent identities (internal).
docs/PHASE3_PARALLEL_PLAN.md
# Operator-only publish runbook — lists the private names it must keep OUT of
# Layer A, so it is itself internal and must never be published.
docs/PUBLISH_ORPHAN_PLAN.md
docs/FAMILY_COUNCIL_OPERATING_MODEL.md
docs/FIRST_30_DAYS.md

# Booth export (git-archive of tracked tree + prebuilt binaries; regenerated, never committed)
booth/
mcps/
